/* src/tables/cow_trivial_rows.def - THE TABLE. Generated by tools/cow/mktable.py from
   ledger/functions.csv and generated/all: one row per entry whose whole body is one of the
   shapes in layout/trivial.h and which the vtable model can name an owner for. Do not edit -
   rerun `python tools/cow/mktable.py --write`. `python tools/cow/mktable.py --check 0x<hex>`
   re-derives a row from the bytes, which is how tools/cow/gate.ps1 keeps it honest.

   Columns: (entry, kind, value, pop, owner). The value is the immediate, the global VA or the
   field offset; pop is what the entry's `ret` cleans; owner is who reaches the address. The
   meaning of every kind is in layout/trivial.h; the only code is src/tables/cow_trivial.c.
*/

